@startuml uc_operation_forwarding
title Use Case: Operate on and Close a Context
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ParticipantPadding 18
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor Client
participant "MediatorImpl" as Mediator
participant "IDataManager" as DataMgr
participant "ContextDataNode" as Node
participant "Handler" as Handler

Client -> Mediator : operation addressed to a context node
Mediator -> DataMgr : get node for client
alt node missing, or not a context node
  Mediator --> Client : kInvalidArgument
else context without a handler
  Mediator --> Client : kInternalError
else
  Mediator -> Node : GetHandler
  Mediator -> Handler : Execute(operation, parameters)
  alt handler succeeds
    Handler --> Mediator : response parameters
    Mediator --> Client : response parameters
  else handler fails
    Handler --> Mediator : daemon error
    Mediator --> Client : error as public code
  end
end

Client -> Mediator : CTX_CLOSE
Mediator -> DataMgr : delete context node
note right
  Deletion also releases the key bound to the context.
  A node that is already absent counts as closed.
end note
Mediator --> Client : success
@enduml
